+### Game mode
+
+For games with mouse-look, add `game=1` to the page's link (`?token=…&game=1`) or
+press the gamepad button in the toolbar. A click on the desktop then locks the mouse
+pointer, and the mouse sends relative motion (`mr,dx,dy`) instead of positions;
+clicks and the wheel still work. Hold W and press P to pause; leaving the lock any
+other way (Esc, switching windows) pauses too. Pausing releases every held key and
+button and stops input until you press Resume; Leave closes the window. The relative
+motion is real on Windows (`SendInput`) and X11 (XTEST); on macOS the cursor moves
+by the delta, clamped to the display, with the motion in the event's delta fields.
+
 ### Login
 
 voxl asks for a password before it shows the desktop or takes input, files or API
